# Ledger API: TypeScript SDK

Customers, invoices, payments and refunds for small businesses.

Zero runtime dependencies. Uses the platform's `fetch` and Web Crypto, so it runs on Node 18+,
browsers and edge runtimes.

## Usage

```ts
import Ledger from 'ledger';

const client = new Ledger({ apiKey: process.env['LEDGER_API_KEY'] });
```

Every credential option falls back to an environment variable:

- `apiKey`: `LEDGER_API_KEY`
- `clientId`: `LEDGER_CLIENT_ID`
- `clientSecret`: `LEDGER_CLIENT_SECRET`

## Environments

Pass `environment` or any `baseURL`, or set `LEDGER_BASE_URL`:

- `production`: https://api.ledger.example (default)
- `sandbox`: https://sandbox.ledger.example

## Requests

Every method takes request options last: `timeout`, `maxRetries`, `headers`, `query`, `body`,
`signal` and `idempotencyKey`. Failed requests (connection errors, 408, 409, 429, 5xx)
are retried twice, honouring `Retry-After`. Every non-GET request carries an
`Idempotency-Key` header that stays the same across retries.

Call `.withResponse()` on any call to get `{ data, response }`.

Set `LEDGER_LOG=debug` to log requests; credentials are redacted.
